backend/app/ml/model_backups/

# The CURRENTLY-LIVE model of each family is tracked, and nothing else.
# Two reasons, both from real incidents:
#   1. A fresh clone had 0 .pkl and 0 registry.json — verified by actually
#      cloning the repo and counting — so CI could not run the model-dependent
#      tests at all.
#   2. This project already lost a live model once: the pre-attendance mid-term
#      version had no backup anywhere (never tracked, direct-overwrite pattern)
#      and was recovered only by chance from an unrelated Docker image. See
#      README, "Mid-semester (partial-progress) prediction".
# Experimental/superseded versions stay ignored (~27MB of them) — reproducible
# from train_model.py, and needed neither to serve nor to test.
# NOTE: these ignore directory *contents* (`dir/*`) rather than the directory
# itself, because git cannot un-ignore a file inside an ignored directory.
backend/app/ml/models/*
!backend/app/ml/models/registry.json
!backend/app/ml/models/model_20260808_110630.pkl
backend/app/ml/models_simulated/*
!backend/app/ml/models_simulated/registry.json
!backend/app/ml/models_simulated/model_20260808_113534.pkl
# SHAP background caches — ~9KB each, required by explain.py at import time.
!backend/app/ml/shap_background_main.pkl
!backend/app/ml/shap_background_simulated.pkl
backend/app/ml/attendance_features.csv
backend/app/ml/column_review_decisions.json
backend/app/ml/ingested_capstone.csv
backend/app/ml/.ingest.lock

